  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\axiom.of.power.set]\nAxiom:\ngiven: A is \\set\nthen:\n. exists: P is \\set\n  suchThat:\n  . forAll: x is \\set\n    then: (x \"in\"? P) \\.iff./ (x \\:set.theoretic.subset?:/ A)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Axiom of Power Set\"\n. description: \"For every set $A$ there is a set $P$ whose members are exactly\n                the subsets of $A$. This power set collects together all of the\n                ways of selecting elements from $A$.\"\nId: \"8557cdb3-e02f-4b75-aed1-3dfd1cdee895\"",
